    "title": "Damped Oscillation Decay",
    "field": "Classical Mechanics / Physics",
    "plotType": "Decaying sinusoid (displacement vs. time)",
    "description": "This plot shows the displacement of an oscillator versus time as its amplitude shrinks under damping, drawing a sinusoid whose peaks fall inside an exponential decay envelope. The rate at which the envelope collapses measures how quickly the system loses energy to friction or drag. It is the canonical way to characterize a damped harmonic oscillator and to extract its damping coefficient and quality factor from a single ring-down measurement.",
