    "whatItTellsYou": "A slowly-shrinking envelope means light (underdamped) damping and a high Q; a rapid collapse means heavy damping. If the motion never crosses zero and just glides back to rest, the system is over- or critically damped. The ratio of successive peak heights gives the logarithmic decrement and hence the damping constant.",
